  "conventions": {
    "uv": "as ground_layout.json: u along the image's columns, v down its rows, one unit per 256 m tile; a rect [u0, v0, u1, v1] or line can run past 1, so draw each again shifted by -1 in u and v",
    "cells": "the surfaces in paint order, a later one over an earlier one; region verge (sidewalk between kerb and lot), apron (paving behind a building), yard (a ring lot behind its building, or a vacant one), core (behind the ring), alley, bed (planting inside a garden); lot is the ground_layout lot index the cell belongs to; a cell can run under a lot, so test a stamp against the lots",
    "lines": "fence or wall (a courtyard or rear wall), cut where it crosses a lot or a street",
    "paths": "worn or paved footpaths as polylines, cut the same way",
    "frame": "the layout lies in the strip's own frame, x along the street, y across it from one centreline to the next, one unit per 256 m; a point (x, y) is uv = origin + x * x_axis + y * y_axis, a turn, and the ground repeats with the tile, so take uv modulo 1"
  },
